===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hɛpˈtæθlɒn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-heptathlon.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|heptathla}}

# {{lb|en|athletics}} An [[athletic]] [[contest]] comprising [[seven]] [[event]]s; contested mostly by [[women]], for whom this is an [[Olympic]] sport.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Frank Litsky|title=Swedish Star Finds Motivation in Variety|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2008/01/26/sports/othersports/26run.html|date=26-01-2008|passage=[Carolina Kluft] has won her last 19 '''heptathlons'''. Only the legendary Jackie Joyner-Kersee has scored higher.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Shauna Farnell|title=An Olympic Hurdle: Why Is the Decathlon Only for Men?|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/07/06/sports/olympics/us-track-field-decathlon-women-heptathlon.html?searchResultPosition=1|date=06-07-2021|passage=For now, Gray and her peers are able to compete for Olympic berths only in the seven-event '''heptathlon''', while the decathlon is restricted to men.}}

